---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Affiliate Disclosure — PrenupAnswers"
  description="How PrenupAnswers makes money: affiliate links, advertising, and why commissions never change our recommendations."
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Affiliate Disclosure</p>
      <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
      <p class="meta">The full, un-buried version.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      In plain terms: <strong>some links on PrenupAnswers are affiliate links.</strong> If you click one and complete
      a purchase, we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you. This is required disclosure under the
      Federal Trade Commission's rules, and we're stating it here instead of burying it in a footer.
    </p>
    <h2>What we affiliate with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Online prenup and postnuptial agreement services</li>
      <li>Legal document platforms (wills, trusts, estate planning)</li>
      <li>Amazon and other retail programs for products we recommend</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What this does NOT change</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>We don't rank by commission.</strong> Recommendations are based on price, state coverage, contract quality, and real user reviews.</li>
      <li><strong>We disclose costs either way.</strong> If the smart move is a $90 DIY route, the article says $90 DIY route.</li>
      <li><strong>We don't accept payment for placements.</strong> No brand buys a "recommended" spot on this site.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Once traffic warrants it, we may display ads served by networks such as Google AdSense or Mediavine. Advertisers
      never influence our editorial conclusions.
    </p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Email hello@prenupanswers.com and we'll answer straight.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
